to a child in the lobby.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and Alexi
were walking in the park.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.198 line:92%
-I'm part of your birth story.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are very much
a part of our birth story.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:10.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have not seen you at all
How have you been?

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've been good.
I've been really good.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.708
I've been here most of the time.
You know, the whole thing.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even oftentimes I would look
into your windows,

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.247 line:92%
thinking you were there, and -

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't looking into
your windows like a creep.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, like a cool guy.
-And then I would see you --

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.087 size:81% position:41%
Yeah, like a cool guys
looks in the window.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they would be darkened
and I would be sad.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.858 line:92%
And I would be upset about that.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I miss you
in the neighborhood.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.261 line:92%
And I would love to see you.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I actually
have had this happen.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, you and I, we are
in show business,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.869
and we know that sometimes
you will have something going on

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
where a car will be sent
to pick you up.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And I was walking by

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
your building,
and I saw one of those cars.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "Oh,
I bet this is for Justin.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.681 line:92%
And maybe I'll wait and say hi."

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I realized
I was the creep,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause the driver
was just looking at me.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm a guy in a mask
who just stopped.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "You know what
I'm gonna..."

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And your Sharpie.
-"I'm gonna keep walking."

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was something, the timing
obviously was not ideal,

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you managed
to make it through.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:14.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
You opened a bar in the city
in 2019.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:18.271
How did you manage through
not, obviously, a great year

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for a bar?

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no,
it was not a great year.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you know, it's --
Look, we were fine

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
with not turning a profit
last year.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
Obviously, like everybody,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was more about
just sort of making sure

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
that everyone
got to keep their job.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
We shut down only
for a couple months, actually.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:40.593 size:84% position:42%
And then Mr. de Blasio
was doing a bang-up job

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.794 size:84% position:42% line:92%
by opening up the city.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let us open again
and serve booze outside,

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
which also is not ideal
in the cold winter months.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, yeah, everyone

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
was basically able
to sort of maintain.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were able
to keep the bar open.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:58.411
So, now, it's wildly open,
and we've almost kind of doubled

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:02.115 size:81% position:41%
the outdoor space now,
which is really fun.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've kind of -- We're quickly
making our way back.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
it was that thing --

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.657
It was actually kind of cool
all the restaurants and bars

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
all kind of started doing,
like -- you know,

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.364
sort of, I guess, collabs,
for lack of a better word,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we'd serve burgers
or pizzas from --

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
a Brooklyn pizza place.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or we'd have, you know --
Yeah, we just -- we would do

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, food and drinks
and stuff.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.009 size:84% position:42%
We were able to keep
the whole thing afloat.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:33.146 size:81% position:41%
-I will say, yesterday
was a very warm night

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
in New York City,
and as I was leaving the show,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
a day after
the CDC basically said

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't have to wear a mas
outside,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
New York felt 100% back,
last night.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, and especially
over where we live,

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
where there's also
a lot of the U's,

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:52.632
the park started to just loo
like a Berlin summer festiva

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something.
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.502
It was so schizophrenic.
People, like, skateboardin

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doing wheelies
and light sticks

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.573 size:88% position:44%
and all the rest of it.
-I felt like an old man,

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I was like,
"I miss the old days,

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the kids
had to stay inside."

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Kids!" [ Laughs ]
-Hey, you let your dog

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
come to the bar.
-All the time, yeah.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we have
very different dogs,

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
but very similar colorings
on our dogs.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.423
-I've only heard about your dog.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's your dog's name again?
-Frisbee.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:22.328 line:92%
And Frisbee doesn't go out much,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she gets cold
right away.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel like our dogs are
like, the same color

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
but very different.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your dog looks like the
dehydrated version of my dog

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you made --
Yeah, that's like --

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you made dog jerky out
of that,

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would look like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:43.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your dog looks like taxidermy
with a broken ear.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.450 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How dare you!
-I kid with Frisbee.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:50.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
Hey, so, this is really cool

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Mosquito Coast,"
it's great.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:58.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not know that your uncle
was Paul Theroux,

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
who wrote this book
40 years ago

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:03.002
and is a wonderful author,
who I love a great deal.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.103 line:92%
And one of the reasons I think

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
it never occurred to me
he was your uncle

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:08.074 size:84% position:42%
is that you say your
last names differently.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.742 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-This is a whole thing.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's not a whole thing
but it's a thing.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.681 size:75% position:38%
You know, he says --
It's a French name.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And originally, when I
check into a hotel in France

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
they say, "Oh, bonjour,
Monsieur 'Teroo.'"

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's got
a hard "T" sound on it.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, I guess,
when he came over,

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.993 line:92%
to be easier, made it "Ther-oo."

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.028 line:92%
And then, I guess, growing up,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
no one really
got my name correctly.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sort of, the neighborhood
chose my name.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm not gonna go up agains
the whole neighborhood,

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they would just say
"Thoreau,"

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:38.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
or teachers
would mispronounce it.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, "Where is Justin
Therux," or whatever.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, wherever it landed, that's
kind of what I stuck with.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it was too late.
And only now

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.947
that we're doing a show together
has this resurfaced

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
as creating a schism
in our family.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did he know this was happenin
behind the scenes?

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:55.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know sometimes, as an author
you're not familiar

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
or up-to-date
with what's happening.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
It looks like

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's something
we cooked up together,

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:04.797
but it was one of those things
that one of my managers said

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:07.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, they're doing
'The Mosquito Coast'?

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:08.868 line:92%
It just popped up on our radar."

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "Oh,
that's interesting,

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.805 line:92%
I'd like to read that script."

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I read it,
and then I said,

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's a really good script
I'd like to do this."

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I met with Neil Cross, an
then I met with Apple.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then --
And then I sort of --

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:26.052
We went down the road, and
I ended up signing up for it

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:28.788
And then I just called --
I got to call him and say,

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Guess what?
Guess what I'm doing with you.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was just sort of
a happy accident.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:36.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it wasn't planne
in that way.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:38.431 size:84% position:42%
-That's just wonderful.
This had been a film

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:41.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
almost, I guess,
like 30 or 40 years ago,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well,
starring Harrison Ford.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is even maybe
a bigger shock to me

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the fact
that Paul is your uncle.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:49.342 line:92%
While you were filming this,

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
you randomly met Harrison Ford
for the first time.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:55.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, totally.
I was in Mexico City

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
and staying at a hotel,
and he happened to come in

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:01.754 size:78% position:39%
to do something else,
and a friend of ours

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:04.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
notified us, "Hey, you kno
Harrison Ford's --"

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.492 size:84% position:42%
or a mutual friend --
that he's in the hotel.

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:09.162
And I thought, "Oh, can we
have dinner or something,

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:09.929 size:75% position:38% line:92%
or a cup of coffee?"

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said,
"Let me put it together."

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they put it together.
And we had this --

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:14.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, one of those
private dining room situations

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we just had
a ton of tacos and tequila

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:22.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just sat and gabbed
and had, like,

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:25.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
a really long, great, slightly
drunken night together.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:27.880
And it was fabulous.
It's exactly what you would want

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.484
a long dinner with Harrison Ford
to be like.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like -- It was just -
He's such a charmer.

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:38.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a lovely man.
-That is fantastic.

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:42.495
And it is very cool that you are
playing the same part as him

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:43.696 size:78% position:39%
And it's always great
to see you, buddy.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope it happens
on the street soon.

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:48.134 size:84% position:42%
-I hope so, too, man.
-Alright, all the best.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:51.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Mosquito Coast" premieres
globally on Apple TV+,

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the first two episode
tomorrow,

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
followed by new episodes
every Friday.

